WEBVTT

00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:16,010
Even before the mastectomy, almost none of my cancer markers came back high.

00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:21,010
I ran four of them, 15 CA, 15-3 was a little high.

00:00:21,010 --> 00:00:27,010
Once in the normal, the next three times, 19. CEA, we're always doing this.

00:00:27,010 --> 00:00:31,010
27-29 was a little high and always normal.

00:00:31,010 --> 00:00:38,010
So I just run the CA 27-29.4.

00:00:39,010 --> 00:00:44,010
I wouldn't because, you know, cancer markers.

00:00:44,010 --> 00:00:54,010
I mean, you know, so cancer markers can be a good way to test progress of your therapy.

00:00:54,010 --> 00:01:02,010
But together, it's not perfect because not all cancers will, will spew out the protein.

00:01:02,010 --> 00:01:06,010
You know, a person could be having a raging stage 4 cancer.

00:01:06,010 --> 00:01:12,010
It's still not spew out any of those proteins and so all their cancer markers are normal.

00:01:12,010 --> 00:01:15,010
So, it's not a perfect test.

00:01:15,010 --> 00:01:19,010
Just like I said, the little test is going to be perfect.

00:01:19,010 --> 00:01:27,010
But, you know, especially if you have basically a full remission diagnosis,

00:01:27,010 --> 00:01:31,010
I would still run those, maybe every three to six months,

00:01:31,010 --> 00:01:44,010
is because if there is metastasis, the metastatic tumor can be, can release a different cancer marker than the initial tumor.

00:01:44,010 --> 00:01:47,010
So you'd hate to miss it.

00:01:47,010 --> 00:01:56,010
And cost-wise, I just, I don't think it's that much different to do that panel than it is to do.

00:01:56,010 --> 00:02:01,010
One or two of them, so.

00:02:01,010 --> 00:02:05,010
I would run, I would run all of them.

00:02:05,010 --> 00:02:08,380
I think that's what we've been doing.

00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:12,380
Of course, if they're all normal, then you can spread out how often you run them.

00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:17,380
So if they're all within your limits, maybe you're only going to just do a scan every six months or something.

00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:27,730
And again, just like every other test, you balance it with, with, you know, other signs and symptoms

00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:29,730
and other lab tests, too.

00:02:29,730 --> 00:02:34,730
So it's, you don't just rely on one test.

